 ## [Unreleased]

+### Fixed
+
+- Codex hook trust diagnosis now compares each stored approval hash with the
+  current normalized hook definition, matching Codex's trust boundary. Managed
+  release path changes are reported as `modified` and factory diagnostics stay
+  degraded until the user reviews the changed Hooks in Codex.
+- Default fresh-thread handoff records are now project-neutral: they use a
+  generic continuation intent and do not inject Throughline development
+  constraints into unrelated repositories.
+- Codex app-server commands now discover the executable bundled or cached by
+  Codex Desktop on Windows and macOS, with `CODEX_CLI_PATH` taking precedence,
+  instead of requiring a separately installed global `codex` command.
+- Codex hook trust diagnosis now accepts TOML literal-string state keys emitted
+  for Windows paths, avoiding a false `0/3 trusted` result after approval.
+- Codex rollout capture now accepts both the legacy `event_msg` conversation /
+  `function_call` tool records and the current Codex App `response_item.message` /
+  `custom_tool_call` records. Host-injected user context such as the Codex
+  `recommended_plugins` and `AGENTS.md` envelopes is excluded from L2. A focused
+  regression fixture and a read-only smoke against a Codex Desktop
+  `0.149.0-alpha.4.1` rollout cover the current shape.
+
